/**
  @page examples-shapeoptimization-index Shape optimization examples
  @brief Use a state solve and a shape derivative to evolve a design boundary.

  The design is an elastic body's material domain. Compliance and an area
  penalty define the objective; the state equation supplies displacement and
  stress. A regularized shape derivative determines the geometry update.

  @tableofcontents

  @section examples-shapeoptimization-start Prerequisites

  The @ref examples-pdes-elasticity "elasticity tutorial" supplies the state
  problem. The @ref guides-shape-optimization "shape optimization guide"
  derives the derivative, descent sign and regularization conventions.
  Both examples use MMG and require a hydrated input mesh from the repository's
  Git LFS resources.

  @section examples-shapeoptimization-route Choose a representation

  Start with direct boundary deformation to follow the state, derivative and
  remeshing steps. Then use the level-set example to study transport and
  reconstruction of a material interface inside a background domain.

  1. @subpage examples-shapeoptimization-simple_cantilever — A cantilever
     with an explicitly displaced boundary and remeshing after each update.
  2. @subpage examples-shapeoptimization-levelset_cantilever — A cantilever
     whose material interface is transported through a signed field and
     reconstructed by MMG.

  @section examples-shapeoptimization-results Assess an update sequence

  Each tutorial provides computed geometry, recorded objectives, output-file
  descriptions and the complete example source. Compare compliance, material
  area and their weighted objective at solved states. Check solver status,
  Jacobian signs and element quality after geometry updates.

  The examples use fixed update budgets. The level-set tutorial also records
  increasing objective steps and a reproduced low-quality triangle after
  interface reconstruction. These measurements guide the choice of step
  acceptance, geometric quality controls and stopping criteria for a new
  application.

  @section examples-shapeoptimization-next Geometry and material fields

  - @ref examples-swift-background "MMG–SWIFT interface fitting" — Isolate
    classification and geometric fitting before coupling a state equation.
  - @ref examples-density_optimization-index "Density optimization" — Vary
    a material coefficient on a fixed domain.

  @m_footernavigation
*/
